{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Missing Yarn Cache Steps Break Offline Install",
    "Explanation": [
      "The step list shows only Spin up environment, Preparing environment variables, Checkout code, then Install Dependencies — there is no \"Restore Cache\" step, because both the restore_cache and save_cache blocks in config.yml are entirely commented out. So no dependency cache existed in ~/.cache/yarn when yarn ran, which is why the offline resolution failed with 'Couldn't find any versions for \"left-pad\" ... (possible versions are \"\")' — the cache was empty. The job log also states 'info No lockfile found.', meaning yarn.lock is not present in the repository; a checksum key can only reference a file that exists, so the key must be derived from package.json (the file that declares the dependencies, e.g. left-pad@1.3.0, and thus changes when dependencies change). Since --offline must stay, the fix is not to drop the flag but to uncomment/enable both the restore_cache (before install) and save_cache (after install, with path ~/.cache/yarn) steps keyed on checksum of package.json — restore alone would never populate the cache, and save alone would never reuse it."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"cache_restored\": false,",
      "  \"checksum_target\": \"package.json\",",
      "  \"fix\": \"enable_restore_and_save_cache\"",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"cache_restored\": false,",
        "  \"checksum_target\": \"package.json\",",
        "  \"fix\": \"enable_restore_and_save_cache\"",
        "}"
      ]
    ],
