{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Green run, but deploy fired on an untagged branch push",
    "Explanation": [
      "The run finished SUCCESS (green), so pipeline_green is true. However, the behaviour is wrong: the commit was an untagged push to branch `koans-09-tag-filters` (pipeline #156, no tag shown), yet `deploy` ran and printed \"Deploy complete\". The requirement says untagged branch pushes must not deploy, so behaviour_correct is false. The root cause is that the workflow declares no `filters` at all, so every job runs on every branch push. Fixing only `deploy` is not enough: in CircleCI, jobs run on branches by default and are skipped for tag pushes unless a `tags` filter is present, and a job cannot run if its `requires` upstream jobs were filtered out. So when `beta-main-0.1.1` is pushed, `build` and `test` would be skipped and `deploy` (which requires `test`) could never run green. Therefore the workflow stanza for all jobs in the chain (build, test, deploy) needs tag filtering, with the tag regex restricted to the beta product (e.g. `only: /^beta-.*/`, plus ignoring branches for deploy) so that `beta-main-0.1.1` produces a green deploying workflow while `alpha-*` tags and untagged branch pushes do not deploy. Filters must go in the workflow job entry, not the job definition, and `requires` alone does not propagate tag filters."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
      "  \"fix\": \"filters_tags_only_beta\",",
      "  \"fix_target_job\": \"all_jobs\",",
      "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
        "  \"fix\": \"filters_tags_only_beta\",",
        "  \"fix_target_job\": \"all_jobs\",",
        "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
        "}"
      ]
    ],
